    <bpmn:process id="W_W1905" name="W1905. In-Store Customer Intercept Survey &amp; Shopper Journey Mapping" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Semi-annual shopper research program
Frequency: Semi-annual; 2-week data collection period
Volume: ~500–1,000 intercept interviews across 10 stores per cycle
Owner: Market Research Analyst
Participants: Market Research Analyst, Research Agency (field interviewers), VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1905 — In-Store Customer Intercept Survey &amp; Shopper Journey Mapping</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1905_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1905_Lane1" name="Market Research Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1905_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1905_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1905_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1905_Lane2" name="Research Agency">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1905_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1905_Lane3" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1905_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1905_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1905_Start5" name="Semi-annual shopper research program">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1905_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1905_Task6" name="Market Research Analyst designs intercept survey and shopper journey study: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Market Research Analyst designs intercept survey and shopper journey study: (a) shopper profile: purpose of visit, frequency, companion type, time spent in store, (b) journey mapping: which departments did they visit? In what order? What was their path through the store?, (c) conversion: did they find what they were looking for? If not, why? Did they buy anything?, (d) basket analysis: what did they buy vs. what they intended to buy?, (e) store experience: signage clarity, department navigation, staff interaction quality, checkout experience, (f) competitor comparison: where else do they shop for home improvement? Why?
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1905_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1905_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1905_Task7" name="Execute fieldwork: (a) engage research agency for trained interviewers at 10…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Execute fieldwork: (a) engage research agency for trained interviewers at 10 stores (5 urban, 5 provincial), (b) 2-week data collection: intercept customers at store exit, (c) observational component: track shopper movement patterns through store (heatmap analysis)
Responsible (R): Research Agency
Accountable (A): Market Research Analyst
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1905_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1905_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1905_Task8" name="Analysis: (a) shopper journey maps: typical paths for DIY vs. trade customers…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Analysis: (a) shopper journey maps: typical paths for DIY vs. trade customers, (b) conversion rate by department: what % of visitors to each department make a purchase?, (c) friction points: where do customers get frustrated or leave without buying?, (d) cross-shop analysis: which competitor stores do BuildRight customers also visit?, (e) recommendations: store layout optimization, signage improvement, department staffing realignment
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1905_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1905_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1905_Task9" name="VP Store Operations and VP Merchandising review findings: (a) incorporate into…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: VP Store Operations and VP Merchandising review findings: (a) incorporate into planogram optimization (W1848), (b) address navigation and signage issues, (c) adjust department staffing based on traffic patterns, (d) consider store layout modifications for high-friction areas
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1905_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1905_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1905_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1905_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1905_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-373 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Satisfaction &amp; Experience Research (PA-44.1).) | - operational: Market Research Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Market Research Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
